---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Notice"
  description="Draft privacy notice for The OC Events Market website and contact by text message."
  noindex
>
  <article class="prose-page">
    <h1>Privacy Notice</h1>
    <p><strong>Owner and legal review required before production launch.</strong></p>
    <p>
      This draft explains the intended website data flow. It does not replace legal advice and must
      be reviewed against the final hosting, analytics, messaging, retention, and business
      practices.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact by text message</h2>
    <p>
      This website does not accept inquiry forms. Selecting a text link asks your device to open its
      usual messaging application with the business number addressed. The QR code is generated
      locally by the website and does not contact a QR code service.
    </p>

    <h2>Information you choose to send</h2>
    <p>
      A message is not sent until you choose to send it in your messaging application. Any text you
      send is handled by your device, carrier or messaging provider, and the business recipient.
      Message content should be used only to review and respond to the conversation, assess
      potential fit, and maintain necessary business records.
    </p>

    <h2>Service providers</h2>
    <p>
      Cloudflare hosts the website and may process ordinary request and security logs. The messaging
      services used by you and the business process texts outside this website. Any future analytics
      service and its terms for processing data must be reflected here before it is enabled.
    </p>

    <h2>Retention and rights</h2>
    <p>
      The owner must approve a retention schedule, deletion process, request contact, and any
      disclosures specific to California that apply to the business. No retention period is invented
      in this draft.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      A verified privacy contact email or mailing address is still required. Until it is supplied,
      this notice cannot be treated as legal copy that is ready for launch.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
